{"id":196717592,"slug":"its-not-my-birthday-so-why-do-you","title":"It's Not My Birthday, So Why Do You Lunge Out At Me?","subtitle":"I'm such a bad liar","post_date":"2026-05-06T23:10:32.796Z","audience":"everyone","type":"newsletter","canonical_url":"https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/p/its-not-my-birthday-so-why-do-you","wordcount":516,"source":"api","fetched_at":"2026-09-13T21:44:01.152Z","body_sha256":"ca30fd87f77c67bbc7f184cf47aa6b837fbe497d352259635fcb1aa62d523366","text_words":531,"complete":true,"body_html":"<p>One of my favorite They Might Be Giants song is called “<a href=\"https://youtu.be/uERCGX61cgE\">It’s Not My Birthday…”</a></p><p>It’s a work of pure hysterical realism genius, before that term was even a thing.</p><p><em>Well, the rain falls down without my help, I’m afraid<a href=\"https://genius.com/32812019/They-might-be-giants-its-not-my-birthday/Well-the-rain-falls-down-without-my-help-im-afraid-and-my-lawn-gets-wet-though-ive-withheld-my-consent\"><br>And my lawn gets wet though I’ve withheld my consent</a><br>When this gray world crumbles like a cake<br>I’ll be hanging from the hope that I’ll never see that recipe again<br><br>[Verse 2]<br>As I walk, I think about a new way to walk<br>As I think, I’m using up the time left to think<br>And this train keeps rolling off the track<br>Tryna act like something else<br>Tryna go where it’s been uninvited<br><br>[Chorus]<br>It’s not my birthday, it’s not today<br>It’s not my birthday, so why do you lunge out at me?<br>When the word comes down, “Never more will be around”<a href=\"https://genius.com/32812212/They-might-be-giants-its-not-my-birthday/When-the-word-comes-down-never-more-will-be-around-though-ill-wish-we-were-there-i-was-less-than-we-could-bear\"><br></a>Though I’ll wish we were there, I was less than we could bear<br>And I’m not the only dust my mother raised<br><br>[Verse 3]<br>So I’m rattling the bars around this drink tank<a href=\"https://genius.com/32812264/They-might-be-giants-its-not-my-birthday/So-im-rattling-the-bars-around-this-drink-tank-discreetly-i-should-pour-through-the-keyhole-or-evaporate-completely-but-thered-be-no-percentage-and-thered-be-no-proof-and-the-sound-upon-the-roof-is-only-water\"><br></a>Discreetly I should pour through the keyhole or evaporate completely<a href=\"https://genius.com/32812264/They-might-be-giants-its-not-my-birthday/So-im-rattling-the-bars-around-this-drink-tank-discreetly-i-should-pour-through-the-keyhole-or-evaporate-completely-but-thered-be-no-percentage-and-thered-be-no-proof-and-the-sound-upon-the-roof-is-only-water\"><br></a>But there’d be no percentage and there’d be no proof<a href=\"https://genius.com/32812264/They-might-be-giants-its-not-my-birthday/So-im-rattling-the-bars-around-this-drink-tank-discreetly-i-should-pour-through-the-keyhole-or-evaporate-completely-but-thered-be-no-percentage-and-thered-be-no-proof-and-the-sound-upon-the-roof-is-only-water\"><br></a>And the sound upon the roof is only water</em></p><p><em>[Verse 1]<br>And the rain falls down without my help, I’m afraid<br>And my lawn gets wet though I’ve withheld my consent<br>When this grey world crumbles like a cake<br>I’ll be hanging from the hope that I’ll never see that recipe again<br><br>[Chorus]<br>It’s not my birthday, it’s not today<br>It’s not my birthday, so why do you lunge out at me?<br>When the word comes down “Never more will be around”<br>Though I’ll wish we were there, I was less than we could bear<br>And I’m not the only dust my mother raised<br>I am not the only dust my mother raised</em></p><div><hr></div><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!WQLo!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F5cbfface-157d-45cf-8ddc-53fa3993f6be_4032x3024.jpeg\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!WQLo!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F5cbfface-157d-45cf-8ddc-53fa3993f6be_4032x3024.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!WQLo!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F5cbfface-157d-45cf-8ddc-53fa3993f6be_4032x3024.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!WQLo!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F5cbfface-157d-45cf-8ddc-53fa3993f6be_4032x3024.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!WQLo!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F5cbfface-157d-45cf-8ddc-53fa3993f6be_4032x3024.jpeg 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!WQLo!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F5cbfface-157d-45cf-8ddc-53fa3993f6be_4032x3024.jpeg\" width=\"452\" height=\"602.5631868131868\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/5cbfface-157d-45cf-8ddc-53fa3993f6be_4032x3024.jpeg&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:1941,&quot;width&quot;:1456,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:452,&quot;bytes&quot;:1805895,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:false,&quot;topImage&quot;:true,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/i/196717592?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F5cbfface-157d-45cf-8ddc-53fa3993f6be_4032x3024.jpeg&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!WQLo!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F5cbfface-157d-45cf-8ddc-53fa3993f6be_4032x3024.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!WQLo!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F5cbfface-157d-45cf-8ddc-53fa3993f6be_4032x3024.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!WQLo!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F5cbfface-157d-45cf-8ddc-53fa3993f6be_4032x3024.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!WQLo!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F5cbfface-157d-45cf-8ddc-53fa3993f6be_4032x3024.jpeg 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" fetchpriority=\"high\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a><figcaption class=\"image-caption\">The Boss, last night.  Presumably about to play happy birthday.</figcaption></figure></div><p>It’s a great song.  Today, however, it is a lie.  I was born into this world on May the 6th. It was 40odd years before this fine day.  It <em>is</em> today.  The lunging out of all humans is…slightly more understandable. They have well wishes to share.  I’ve written about my birthday before…a sampler:</p><div class=\"digest-post-embed\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;nodeId&quot;:&quot;e6caaa2e-d266-411a-8b16-cd0ffcd58be0&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;I've written about birthdays before. Today is mine. These bring up feelings that are mixed, in adulthood. I haven't had a birthday party for about a decade. I even had someone offered to throw one for me this year, but I ended up on a work trip, and she ended up grieving the impending loss of her mother.&quot;,&quot;cta&quot;:&quot;Read full story&quot;,&quot;showBylines&quot;:true,&quot;showDescription&quot;:true,&quot;showImage&quot;:true,&quot;size&quot;:&quot;md&quot;,&quot;isEditorNode&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;It's Not My Birthday.&quot;,&quot;publishedBylines&quot;:[{&quot;id&quot;:2277375,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Owen Scott Muir, M.D, DFAACAP&quot;,&quot;bio&quot;:&quot;Dr. Owen Scott Muir, M.D., DFAACAP is the Chief Medical Officer of Radial &amp; Neurolief. He's a graduate of Amherst College, Child, Adolescent, and Adult Psychiatrist, and a prolific writer and podcaster. https://www.meetradial.com for more.&quot;,&quot;photo_url&quot;:&quot;https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fbucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F1c03f44d-4506-4843-989f-0d38e66c6946_400x400.jpeg&quot;,&quot;is_guest&quot;:false,&quot;bestseller_tier&quot;:100}],&quot;post_date&quot;:&quot;2025-05-06T18:50:01.492Z&quot;,&quot;cover_image&quot;:&quot;https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!yAx0!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6f03581e-9a28-4cf5-b194-f8c3672931a7_4032x3024.jpeg&quot;,&quot;cover_image_alt&quot;:null,&quot;canonical_url&quot;:&quot;https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/p/its-not-my-birthday&quot;,&quot;section_name&quot;:null,&quot;video_upload_id&quot;:null,&quot;id&quot;:162975902,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;newsletter&quot;,&quot;reaction_count&quot;:13,&quot;comment_count&quot;:10,&quot;publication_id&quot;:355550,&quot;publication_name&quot;:&quot;The Frontier Psychiatrists &quot;,&quot;publication_logo_url&quot;:&quot;https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!oO3w!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fbucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F997b8496-9b4d-43c2-b393-6f8a77945b00_1080x1080.png&quot;,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:false,&quot;youtube_url&quot;:null,&quot;show_links&quot;:null,&quot;feed_url&quot;:null}\"></div><div class=\"digest-post-embed\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;nodeId&quot;:&quot;9abe766d-7ecb-419a-9706-e7eb59192687&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;I have turned 45 today. I hate my birthday. I'm not sure that it's so much the day, but the date. May 6 is a perfectly good day, unless, of course, you would like to do something nice on your birthday. As a dual board-certified child and adult psychiatrist, I've done a lot of years of school. May is a beautiful month. Spring is a lovely time. It is als…&quot;,&quot;cta&quot;:&quot;Read full story&quot;,&quot;showBylines&quot;:true,&quot;showDescription&quot;:true,&quot;showImage&quot;:true,&quot;size&quot;:&quot;md&quot;,&quot;isEditorNode&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;It Is My Birthday&quot;,&quot;publishedBylines&quot;:[{&quot;id&quot;:2277375,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Owen Scott Muir, M.D, DFAACAP&quot;,&quot;bio&quot;:&quot;Dr. Owen Scott Muir, M.D., DFAACAP is the Chief Medical Officer of Radial &amp; Neurolief. He's a graduate of Amherst College, Child, Adolescent, and Adult Psychiatrist, and a prolific writer and podcaster. https://www.meetradial.com for more.&quot;,&quot;photo_url&quot;:&quot;https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fbucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F1c03f44d-4506-4843-989f-0d38e66c6946_400x400.jpeg&quot;,&quot;is_guest&quot;:false,&quot;bestseller_tier&quot;:100}],&quot;post_date&quot;:&quot;2024-05-06T12:29:18.118Z&quot;,&quot;cover_image&quot;:&quot;https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!sdI2!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F46cd6dfc-e34d-4e31-ba69-91d86687f279.heic&quot;,&quot;cover_image_alt&quot;:null,&quot;canonical_url&quot;:&quot;https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/p/it-is-my-birthday&quot;,&quot;section_name&quot;:null,&quot;video_upload_id&quot;:null,&quot;id&quot;:144359405,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;newsletter&quot;,&quot;reaction_count&quot;:6,&quot;comment_count&quot;:9,&quot;publication_id&quot;:355550,&quot;publication_name&quot;:&quot;The Frontier Psychiatrists &quot;,&quot;publication_logo_url&quot;:&quot;https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!oO3w!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fbucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F997b8496-9b4d-43c2-b393-6f8a77945b00_1080x1080.png&quot;,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:false,&quot;youtube_url&quot;:null,&quot;show_links&quot;:null,&quot;feed_url&quot;:null}\"></div><div class=\"digest-post-embed\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;nodeId&quot;:&quot;a2f89785-ea9f-487e-ba20-86429e25df60&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;I won a grant years back to produce a podcast series from NYU’s Rudin Master Scholars Program in Ethics and Humanities. I am proud of that work. This episode never made it on the air. It is presented for your consideration. Suicide is discussed, frankly. Both my friend and guest, Lara J. Cox, M.S., M.D, and I discussed extensively that her&quot;,&quot;cta&quot;:&quot;Listen now&quot;,&quot;showBylines&quot;:true,&quot;showDescription&quot;:true,&quot;showImage&quot;:true,&quot;size&quot;:&quot;md&quot;,&quot;isEditorNode&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;The Once-Suicidal Psychiatrist...A Self-Disclosure, Deferred.&quot;,&quot;publishedBylines&quot;:[{&quot;id&quot;:2277375,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Owen Scott Muir, M.D, DFAACAP&quot;,&quot;bio&quot;:&quot;Dr. Owen Scott Muir, M.D., DFAACAP is the Chief Medical Officer of Radial &amp; Neurolief. He's a graduate of Amherst College, Child, Adolescent, and Adult Psychiatrist, and a prolific writer and podcaster. https://www.meetradial.com for more.&quot;,&quot;photo_url&quot;:&quot;https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fbucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F1c03f44d-4506-4843-989f-0d38e66c6946_400x400.jpeg&quot;,&quot;is_guest&quot;:false,&quot;bestseller_tier&quot;:100}],&quot;post_date&quot;:&quot;2023-10-17T16:38:13.759Z&quot;,&quot;cover_image&quot;:&quot;https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!DkdA!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa649bc22-19d9-4f3e-8edb-a5e3b77259fb_4032x3024.jpeg&quot;,&quot;cover_image_alt&quot;:null,&quot;canonical_url&quot;:&quot;https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/p/the-once-suicidal-psychiatrista-self&quot;,&quot;section_name&quot;:null,&quot;video_upload_id&quot;:null,&quot;id&quot;:137989395,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;podcast&quot;,&quot;reaction_count&quot;:5,&quot;comment_count&quot;:2,&quot;publication_id&quot;:355550,&quot;publication_name&quot;:&quot;The Frontier Psychiatrists &quot;,&quot;publication_logo_url&quot;:&quot;https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!oO3w!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fbucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F997b8496-9b4d-43c2-b393-6f8a77945b00_1080x1080.png&quot;,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;youtube_url&quot;:null,&quot;show_links&quot;:null,&quot;feed_url&quot;:null}\"></div><p>But, like all cyclic things, It’s back.  Birthdays are relaping and remitting, and the only cure is worse than the disease.</p><p>This year, <span class=\"mention-wrap\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Lila&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:37262322,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:null,&quot;photo_url&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/3e42498b-2a65-4cc0-a072-8608831166d9_2240x3360.jpeg&quot;,&quot;uuid&quot;:&quot;cc756706-6de9-4172-a8df-5c44355cbf0d&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"MentionToDOM\"></span> offered to throw me a party.  I didn’t have the time.  I’ll get to it next year.  How important could it be?</p><p>I know, I know.</p><p>I’ll invite my readers to A party, if not MY birthday party.  It’s FREE for my readers.  Just use the code “FREE.”  Clever, I know.</p><p>It’s called RAMHT!  It’s on May 16th.</p><div><hr></div><h2><strong>The Live-Action Version of this Newsletter, RAMHT 2026 SF, is coming up on May 16th, 2026!</strong></h2><p>Get a ticket now—it’s free if you ask. Just email us at <a href=\"http://ramhtevents@gmail.com/\">ramhtevents@gmail.com</a> for your free code.</p><p class=\"button-wrapper\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://www.eventbrite.com/e/ramht-apa-2026-san-francisco-tickets-1983465503715?utm-campaign=social&amp;utm-content=attendeeshare&amp;utm-medium=discovery&amp;utm-term=listing&amp;utm-source=cp&amp;aff=ebdsshcopyurl&amp;keep_tld=true&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Get Tickets to RAMHT 2026 SF&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:null,&quot;class&quot;:&quot;button-wrapper&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"ButtonCreateButton\"><a class=\"button primary button-wrapper\" href=\"https://www.eventbrite.com/e/ramht-apa-2026-san-francisco-tickets-1983465503715?utm-campaign=social&amp;utm-content=attendeeshare&amp;utm-medium=discovery&amp;utm-term=listing&amp;utm-source=cp&amp;aff=ebdsshcopyurl&amp;keep_tld=true\"><span>Get Tickets to RAMHT 2026 SF</span></a></p><div><hr></div><p>For my birthday, you get a present!</p><p>Thanks for reading, as always.</p><p class=\"button-wrapper\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/subscribe?&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Subscribe now&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:null,&quot;class&quot;:null}\" data-component-name=\"ButtonCreateButton\"><a class=\"button primary\" href=\"https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/subscribe?\"><span>Subscribe now</span></a></p><p class=\"button-wrapper\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/p/its-not-my-birthday-so-why-do-you?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email&utm_content=share&action=share&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Share&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:null,&quot;class&quot;:null}\" data-component-name=\"ButtonCreateButton\"><a class=\"button primary\" href=\"https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/p/its-not-my-birthday-so-why-do-you?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email&utm_content=share&action=share\"><span>Share</span></a></p><p>If you’d like ot hear my music It’s <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCmJlYKaDpFUCfCnl3C33fIw\">here on youtube</a>, or <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/0h2ENRw6OxwFuSpMXCxbp7?si=VrtL9D3_Smu9dW9DdLVqbw\">here on Spotify.</a>  Listen, as your gift to me.</p><p></p>","text":"One of my favorite They Might Be Giants song is called “ It’s Not My Birthday…”\n\nIt’s a work of pure hysterical realism genius, before that term was even a thing.\n\nWell, the rain falls down without my help, I’m afraid\nAnd my lawn gets wet though I’ve withheld my consent\nWhen this gray world crumbles like a cake\nI’ll be hanging from the hope that I’ll never see that recipe again\n\n[Verse 2]\nAs I walk, I think about a new way to walk\nAs I think, I’m using up the time left to think\nAnd this train keeps rolling off the track\nTryna act like something else\nTryna go where it’s been uninvited\n\n[Chorus]\nIt’s not my birthday, it’s not today\nIt’s not my birthday, so why do you lunge out at me?\nWhen the word comes down, “Never more will be around”\nThough I’ll wish we were there, I was less than we could bear\nAnd I’m not the only dust my mother raised\n\n[Verse 3]\nSo I’m rattling the bars around this drink tank\nDiscreetly I should pour through the keyhole or evaporate completely\nBut there’d be no percentage and there’d be no proof\nAnd the sound upon the roof is only water\n\n[Verse 1]\nAnd the rain falls down without my help, I’m afraid\nAnd my lawn gets wet though I’ve withheld my consent\nWhen this grey world crumbles like a cake\nI’ll be hanging from the hope that I’ll never see that recipe again\n\n[Chorus]\nIt’s not my birthday, it’s not today\nIt’s not my birthday, so why do you lunge out at me?\nWhen the word comes down “Never more will be around”\nThough I’ll wish we were there, I was less than we could bear\nAnd I’m not the only dust my mother raised\nI am not the only dust my mother raised\n\nThe Boss, last night. Presumably about to play happy birthday.\n\nIt’s a great song. Today, however, it is a lie. I was born into this world on May the 6th. It was 40odd years before this fine day. It is today. The lunging out of all humans is…slightly more understandable. They have well wishes to share. I’ve written about my birthday before…a sampler:\n\nBut, like all cyclic things, It’s back. Birthdays are relaping and remitting, and the only cure is worse than the disease.\n\nThis year, offered to throw me a party. I didn’t have the time. I’ll get to it next year. How important could it be?\n\nI know, I know.\n\nI’ll invite my readers to A party, if not MY birthday party. It’s FREE for my readers. Just use the code “FREE.” Clever, I know.\n\nIt’s called RAMHT! It’s on May 16th.\n\nThe Live-Action Version of this Newsletter, RAMHT 2026 SF, is coming up on May 16th, 2026!\n\nGet a ticket now—it’s free if you ask. Just email us at ramhtevents@gmail.com for your free code.\n\nGet Tickets to RAMHT 2026 SF\n\nFor my birthday, you get a present!\n\nThanks for reading, as always.\n\nSubscribe now\n\nShare\n\nIf you’d like ot hear my music It’s here on youtube , or here on Spotify. Listen, as your gift to me."}